{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    The sequence is defined with fib4(0)=0, fib4(1)=0, fib4(2)=2, fib4(3)=0,\n    and fib4(n) = fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4) for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n    elif n < 0:\n        # Based on the problem definition, n is expected to be non-negative.\n        # Raising a ValueError for negative input is appropriate.\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    else:\n        # Initialize the first four values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n        a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0\n\n        # Iteratively compute fib4(k) for k from 4 up to n\n        for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n            next_fib4 = a + b + c + d\n            # Shift the window: (fib4(k-3), fib4(k-2), fib4(k-1), fib4(k))\n            a, b, c, d = b, c, d, next_fib4\n        return d"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'x' must be an integer.\")\n    if not isinstance(base, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'base' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Number must be non-negative.\")\n    if not (2 <= base <= 9):\n        raise ValueError(\"Base must be between 2 and 9, inclusive.\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result = []\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        result.append(str(remainder))\n        current_x //= base\n\n    return \"\".join(reversed(result))"}
